<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chilean Civil War of 1829–1830</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1829">1829</a>–<a href="/years/1830">1830</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chilean Civil War of 1829–1830 was fought between the liberals, known as pipiolos, and the conservatives, known as pelucones, after disputed elections in 1829. The conservative army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joaquin-prieto">Joaquín Prieto</a> defeated the liberal forces under Ramón Freire at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lircay">Battle of Lircay</a> in April 1830. The victory began three decades of conservative rule shaped by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-portales">Diego Portales</a> and the constitution of 1833.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chilean-civil-war-of-1829-1830.jpg" alt="Chilean Civil War of 1829–1830" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dirk Jansz van Santen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas_Van_der_Hagen-KW1049B13_089-CHILI.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
